<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Typo</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>typo
</pre>
<p>Found a spelling mistake or a garbled sentence in a room, on a monster or 
an object, or in a help page? Tell the builders. Type typo and press 
enter, and the editor opens, as when you write a letter at the post 
office. Write what is wrong, up to about 4000 characters, and close the 
editor with @ on a line of its own. A single word or nothing at all is 
thrown away. If you use a client with triggers that echo text, turn them 
off first.
</p><p>Your report is saved together with your name and the room you are in, 
and a copy is posted to the game's Discord. So send it from the room 
where you found the typo if you can; if that's too dangerous, from the 
nearest safe room, and say where. Don't send it from inside a tent or a 
boat, unless the typo is on that. If it is on an object, copy its name 
exactly, so that it can be found.
</p><p>If the mistake changes how the game plays, report it with <a cmd='#'>Help Bug</a> 
instead.
</p><p>Example:
</p>
<pre>42h&gt; typo
] The sign in the bakery says "fresh brad".
] @
Thank you. They will be corrected.
</pre>
<p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Bug</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Idea</a>
</pre>




</div>